<title>USA: CCC sets 1997 tobacco assessment.</title>
<headline>CCC sets 1997 tobacco assessment.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department's Commodity Credit Corporation on Wednesday announced a no-net-cost assessment of $0.24 per pound for the 1997 crop of burley tobacco.</p>
<p>Producers and purchasers will each pay $0.12 per pound, the CCC said.</p>
<p>The no-net-cost assessment plus a previously announced tobacco marketing assessment of $0.88 per pound means that a total of $0.02 per pound will be collected on each pound of burley tobacco marketed from the 1997 crop, the CCC said.</p>
</text>
